@startuml qwen3tts-speedup
title <b>qwen3tts: what buys 6.9x realtime</b>\ntwo corpora, 1612-4838 words, 100-203 segments, one M4 / 16 GB, default settings

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam titleFontSize 15
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #6B7A88
  BackgroundColor #EDF1F5
}
skinparam noteFontSize 12

rectangle "text -> segments" as SEG
rectangle "ICL prompt\nref codes + spk" as PROMPT
rectangle "**scheduler**\n48 lanes, longest-first" as SCHED #DDF3E0
rectangle "**talker**\n0.105-0.110  (74%)" as TALKER #DDF3E0
rectangle "**codec**\n0.038-0.042  (26%)" as CODEC #DDF3E0
rectangle "24 kHz WAV\n**0.144-0.148 = 6.8-6.9x**" as WAV #D6E9F8

SEG --> PROMPT
PROMPT --> SCHED
SCHED --> TALKER : "48 lanes"
TALKER --> CODEC : "[T, 16] codes"
CODEC --> WAV

note right of SCHED #DDF3E0
  shape buckets
  length sort, <b>longest-first</b>
  chunk to 48
end note

note right of TALKER #DDF3E0
  f16 <b>by default</b>   7.4x vs q8_0's 1.1x
  <b>decode-shaped GEMM</b> 1.08-1.46x vs candle
  batched decode     48 lanes, longest-first
  shed finished tail  68-70% -> 79-90% useful
  <b>cut a babbling lane</b> one group 230 -> 154 steps
  shed in 8s         one width set, not 48
  prefill in 8s      748 MB -> 94 MB of scores
  in-place KV        -112 MB/step
  folded tables      -126 MB/frame
end note

note right of CODEC #DDF3E0
  one call per utterance
  300 + 25 frame chunks
  uniform span, padded right
  <b>taps gathered inside the GEMM</b> 1.70x
  <b>transposed conv as one conv</b> 2.14x
end note

note left of SCHED #FBDDDD
  <b>cliff past 48 lanes</b>
  peak goes 12.7 -> 15.8 GB from 48
  to 64, spread across the run rather
  than in one buffer. Four ways of
  freeing it are in reference.md
end note

note left of TALKER #FDEBD0
  <i>beyond 7x</i>
  refill <b>interior</b> lanes
  (a tail is shed; a lane that
  finishes mid-batch is not)
end note

note left of CODEC #FDEBD0
  <i>beyond 7x</i>
  torch-parity kernels
end note

note bottom of WAV #FFFDF0
  |= corpus |= segs |= was (24) |= 48 lanes |= <b>shipped</b> |= |
  | Pixel Watch article, 4838w | 203 | | 0.193 | <b>0.144</b> | <b>6.9x</b> |
  | chapter.txt, 1612w | 100 | 0.260 | 0.186 | <b>0.148</b> | <b>6.8x</b> |

  peak footprint 12.5-13.0 GB, from 14.2-14.8. Quality checked on the audio, not the codes,
  because two of these move the logits and a sampled model then takes a different path:
  WER <b>0.036</b> against the release before it, median F0 175.8 Hz and LTAS cosine 0.9974
  against the clip the voice was cloned from. The fused conv is bit-identical to what it
  replaced, across all 42,454,560 samples.

  Memory is candle's Metal pool, which keys buffers by size and releases none, so most wins
  here are a *shape* removed rather than bytes shaved.

  Per lane, in isolation, cost is still falling at 64: 1.615 ms at 48 against 1.460, because
  64 fills the 8x8 matrix tiles 48 leaves ragged. The wall is memory, not arithmetic.
  green measured, amber projected
end note

@enduml
